{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start, you should join the team and agree on the team's domain."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly triggers the init node and describes the initial start/join-team actions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once that is done, create a process model and check it."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct correspondence to the model creation and checking step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4",
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the process model is \"NOT OK\", then assign negative points."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the conditional check (modeled as action), the XOR branch, the positive guard, and the resulting action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "action:n7",
        "guard:b2->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is still \"NOT OK\", assign negative points again."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the secondary check, decision branch, guard, and repeat penalty assignment faithfully."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->c1",
        "guard:b2->c1",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the process is okay, you can continue with it."
      ],
      "justification": "The 'okay' guards route to the converge node, which leads directly to the continuation action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:b6->n10",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are any issues, fix them in the next session and extend the process to levels 2 and 3."
      ],
      "justification": "The AND gateway branch, descriptive label, and action exactly mirror the issue-fixing instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11",
        "label:b6->n11",
        "guard:b3->n12",
        "action:n12",
        "guard:b3->c2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you need to check the process and assign points, continue with the process. If you need to analyze the field of study, assign roles in the team."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n11 summarizes the fork conditions, which are then correctly split by branch b3, routed via guards/labels, executed in n12, and rejoined at c2."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the process is okay, continue with the process and perform work according to your assigned role."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase preserving the continuation and role-based work instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Check the progress and consult any problems that arise."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully restates the progress review and consultation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15",
        "guard:b4->n16",
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the project is accepted, present it."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the acceptance check, branch, positive guard, and presentation action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b4->n18",
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If not, continue working according to your role."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the rejection path guard and the corresponding continued-work action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n19",
        "action:n20",
        "guard:b5->n21",
        "guard:b5->n22",
        "action:n22"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the project is accepted, present it again."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately captures the re-presentation step, second acceptance check, branch, and dual outcomes."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n21",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, present the project and the process will come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the final presentation and termination. Redundant end nodes/action n17 are included as they do not alter behavior."
    }
  ],
